{"conversation_id":"d7c1ab74-5e11-4d3a-824b-f6296e917cde","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Root Cause\nIn [`pkg/cache.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/cache.py#L4-L5), `_key(spec)` generated cache keys using `tuple(spec.items())`. In Python, dictionary items preserve insertion order, so dictionaries with identical key-value pairs inserted in different orders (e.g., `{\"region\": \"eu\", \"tier\": \"gold\"}` and `{\"tier\": \"gold\", \"region\": \"eu\"}`) yielded different cache key tuples, causing cache lookups to miss.\n\n### Fixes Applied\n1. **[`pkg/cache.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/cache.py#L4-L5)**: Updated `_key` to sort the items before converting to a tuple:\n   ```python\n   def _key(spec):\n       return tuple(sorted(spec.items()))\n   ```\n2. **[`pkg/parser.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/parser.py)**: Implemented the missing [`parse_duration`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/parser.py#L14-L22) function required by the test suite.\n\n### Verification\nRan the entire test suite (`pytest -v`): all 8 tests in `test_cache.py`, `test_parser.py`, and `test_smoke.py` pass without modifying any test files.\n","duration_seconds":60.9006645,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":190391,"output_tokens":4702,"thinking_tokens":2641,"cache_read_tokens":230646,"total_tokens":195093}}
